      "defines": [
        "optics-m4-crossed-polarizers"
      ],
      "body": "Crossed polarizers are a polarizer and analyzer whose transmission axes are perpendicular, so the analyzer extinguishes the light.",
      "points": [
        "The polarized light from P is extinguished by A.",
        "Malus' law (Eq. 20.10) gives zero at 90°.",
        "A further 90° turn restores maximum intensity."
      ],
